  "summary": "Malicious code in accounts-limits (npm)",
  "details": "When required, the package downloads a binary payload from Cloudflare Workers C2 infrastructure (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS GET /pkg/package, with a DNS-based fallback using TXT record chunked queries through c[.]tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003crandom\u003e (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003crandom\u003e.exe on Windows) and executed as a detached background process. A lockfile at /tmp/.analytics_state prevents re-execution within a ~6-hour window. The package name \"accounts-limits\" is a decoy with no relation to its behaviour.",
